opennyai_summary.decision:
2. In this Criminal Revision Application, the applicant herein original accused has prayed to release him on bail by suspending the sentence imposed by the learned Third Additional Sessions Judge, At Visnagar, vide judgment and order passed in Criminal Appeal No.4 of 2012 (Old Criminal Case No.59 of 2012) dated 19.1.2017, whereby the learned Second Additional Judicial Magistrate First Class, has confirmed the judgment and order passed by the learned Third Additional Chief Judicial Magistrate, Visnagar, in Criminal Case No.29 of 2005 dated 29.5.2012, whereby learned trial Judge has convicted and sentenced the applicant for the offence punishable under Sections 7(1), 7(5) and 16(1)(a)(1) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act.
He, therefore, prays to grant the bail to the applicant by suspending the sentence till disposal of the present Revision Application.
5. Considering the overall facts and circumstances of the case and sentence imposed by the courts belows, the applicant is required to be enlarged on bail.
